---
description:
  Each subgraph sets its own title position with titlePosition, one for each of the six
  positions, and the last keeps the default at the top in the middle. A subgraph's position
  does not pass to the subgraph nested in it (mermaid-js/mermaid#2977).
---
flowchart TD
    subgraph tl [Top left]
        a1[First node] --> a2[Second node]
    end
    subgraph tc [Top center]
        b1[First node] --> b2[Second node]
    end
    subgraph tr [Top right]
        c1[First node] --> c2[Second node]
    end
    subgraph bl [Bottom left]
        d1[First node] --> d2[Second node]
    end
    subgraph bc [Bottom center]
        e1[First node] --> e2[Second node]
    end
    subgraph br [Bottom right]
        f1[First node] --> f2[Second node]
        subgraph inner [Nested keeps the default]
            f3[Third node]
        end
    end
    subgraph plain [Default]
        g1[First node] --> g2[Second node]
    end
    tl@{ titlePosition: top-left }
    tc@{ titlePosition: top-center }
    tr@{ titlePosition: top-right }
    bl@{ titlePosition: bottom-left }
    bc@{ titlePosition: bottom-center }
    br@{ titlePosition: bottom-right }
